<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H1
/P 92 0 R
/T (The storyboard was one of the first things the group created. Its job was to map out the emotional journey of the piece  from emptiness, through life and connection, and finally to collapse. Before any of the technical work came together, the storyboard gave everyone a shared sense of how the experience should feel and where it was going dramatically.)
/E (The storyboard was one of the first things the group created. Its job was to map out the emotional journey of the piece  from emptiness, through life and connection, and finally to collapse. Before any of the technical work came together, the storyboard gave everyone a shared sense of how the experience should feel and where it was going dramatically.)
/Pg 15 0 R
/K [12]
>>
endobj
165 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H1
/P 92 0 R
/T (As the project developed, the interaction model grew richer than the storyboard originally suggested. Rather than only responding to combinations, the system was built to recognise each individual cuboid on its own. This gave the audience something more exploratory  they could discover what each celestial body looked and sounded like alone before starting to connect them.)
/E (As the project developed, the interaction model grew richer than the storyboard originally suggested. Rather than only responding to combinations, the system was built to recognise each individual cuboid on its own. This gave the audience something more exploratory  they could discover what each celestial body looked and sounded like alone before starting to connect them.)
/Pg 15 0 R
/K [13]
>>
endobj
