187 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 95 0 R
/E (David Rokeby's Very Nervous System is one of the most important works in the history of interactive art. Using cameras and synthesisers, he built a system that turned body movement directly into sound. What stayed with us was his belief that the body not a button or a screen should be the instrument. He wanted the interface to feel as invisible as possible, so that interaction felt natural rather than mechanical. Our project shares that ambition. The cuboids are meant to feel like objects worth picking up and handling, not like input devices. The interactivity should feel discovered, not operated.)
/Pg 18 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
188 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
