207 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 97 0 R
/E (EEach group member built one cuboid using a laser cutter, cutting panels from 3mm MDF sheet and assembling them into a 100mm cube. The outer faces were fitted with copper contact points, so that when two cuboids are pressed together, they conduct electricity between them.)
/Pg 20 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
208 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 97 0 R
/E (Inside each cuboid, a network of resistors was wired across the faces and crucially, each cuboid was given its own unique resistor value. This means the system can identify not just how many cuboids are connected, but exactly which one is present at any moment. The Star, Earth, Moon, and Black Hole can each be recognised individually, so the right visuals and audio trigger no matter what order they are placed in.)
/Pg 20 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
