228 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 99 0 R
/E (A single continuous music track plays throughout the entire experience Solar System Ambience | Space Sounds & Lo-fi Vibes, sourced from YouTube. Rather than switching tracks for each state, the music acts as a constant backdrop, an unbroken thread running from the void, through the building of the solar system, and into its collapse. What changes is not the music itself, but the audience's relationship to it.)
/Pg 22 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
229 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 99 0 R
/E (The key audio moment is a volume dip. Every time a new cuboid is placed and the circuit changes, the music briefly lowers before returning to full volume. This was implemented in TouchDesigner by detecting the moment a channel value changes and triggering a short fade-down and fade-up on the audio output. It is subtle, but it matters it gives each placement a felt pause, a breath, as if the universe briefly holds still in response to being touched.)
/Pg 22 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
