250 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 102 0 R
/E (Working through this project made us think a lot more carefully about what interactivity actually means. It's easy to assume that if something responds to input, it's interactive but what we found is that the response needs to feel meaningful, not just technically functional. The hardest part was taking raw voltage numbers from the Arduino and turning them into something an audience would actually care about.)
/Pg 25 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
251 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 102 0 R
/E (The volume dip on each placement is one of the decisions we're most happy with. It wasn't in the original plan it came out of testing. Without it, placing a cube felt like nothing. With it, every placement had a moment of stillness, like something was genuinely happening in the room. It made the physical action feel connected to what was appearing on screen.)
/Pg 25 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
252 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 102 0 R
/E (The decision to make the Black Hole the final, destructive element was something we talked about a lot as a group. It means the experience ends on a dark note the audience destroys what they built. But we felt that was more interesting and more honest than wrapping things up positively. The whole point is that the audience makes that choice themselves. That felt too important to change.)
/Pg 25 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
253 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/P 102 0 R
/T (Conceptual Reflections)
/E (Conceptual Reflections)
/Pg 25 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
