256 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 103 0 R
/E (The biggest problem we ran into was getting the cuboids to steady control the switching behaviour in TouchDesigner. This became the central issue on presentation day.)
/Pg 26 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
257 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 103 0 R
/E (The signal from the Arduino was arriving correctly we could see the channel values updating inside the patch but the switch logic that was supposed to trigger the right visual state was not firing reliably. At one point we had to bypass the cuboids entirely and switch states manually by typing values into the patch. That was the opposite of what the project was meant to be.)
/Pg 26 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
258 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 103 0 R
/E (The root cause was in the Switch node configuration. The incoming values needed to be correctly mapped before they could drive the switch, and this had not been tested under real conditions beforehand. Once we adjusted the channel expressions in TouchDesigner, the cuboids worked cleanly as intended.)
/Pg 26 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
259 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 103 0 R
/E (This taught us the difference between a system that works in parts and one that works as a whole. Every component had been tested individually, but we had not done enough end-to-end testing before the day. In future, we would set aside dedicated time for full integration testing well in advance.A secondary issue was the copper contact points between cuboids slight misalignment could cause readings to fluctuate. A future version might use magnetic or gold-plated connectors for a more stable connection.)
/Pg 26 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
260 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 103 0 R
/E (Despite these challenges, the system worked during the final presentation. The moment the cuboids took control of the screen was one of the most satisfying points of the whole project.)
/Pg 26 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
